  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\n\nThunderstorms continue to move across the region. Due to the\ngenerally west to east motion, flash flooding will continue to be a\nconcern overnight. Due to this, continued the flood watch for flash\nflooding.  With shear and strong winds with this system, damaging \nwinds and the potential for tornadoes will continue to be a concern. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2)\n\nAfter some showers and isolated thunderstorms on Thursday, dry\nconditions are expected for Friday. Precipitation chances return for\nSaturday. There is some variability with this system which has kept\nprecipitation chances lower, however there is the potential for\nshowers and storms during the day. There is more model agreement on\nSunday with widespread precipitation moving through. There will be\nthe potential for some residual showers and storms Monday morning.",
